            "page": 10,
            "type": "image",
            "title": "AI Reinvents Computer Graphics",
            "excerpt": "With neural rendering and DLSS, AI predicts pixels instead of computing them directly.",
            "crop": [
              0,
              0,
              1,
              1
            ],
            "pageSize": [
              1188.0,
              774.0
            ],
            "pageImage": "/assets/product-documents/nvidia-graphics-page.webp",
            "regionImage": "/assets/product-documents/nvidia-graphics-region.webp",
            "imageSize": [
              2200,
              1434
            ],
            "regionSize": [
              2200,
              1434
            ],
            "pageText": [
              "GeForce brought AI to the world. Now AI has come home to GeForce.",
              "Computer graphics is no longer limited by traditional rendering.",
              "With neural rendering and DLSS, AI predicts pixels instead of computing them directly.",
              "For every pixel we render, AI generates the rest in real time.",
              "Neural networks now run alongside shaders and ray tracing cores. AI does not replace graphics. It enhances it.",
              "In the era of neural rendering, graphics is learned."
            ],
            "summary": "The Annual Review's graphics example illustrates a separate application of AI: neural rendering and DLSS predict pixels alongside traditional rendering."
          }
        ],
        "sha256": "0e725ba048221539dca3eb1a4e70febfcbb785e9afb96cd3ff0b035d7d734e5c",
